WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.782
You may hear modern data described using the three Vs: volume, velocity, and variety.

00:00:05.782 --> 00:00:11.602
Volume is about scale. Velocity is about how quickly data arrives or must be processed.

00:00:11.602 --> 00:00:14.267
Variety is about the different forms of data.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:17.042
This module focuses mainly on variety.

00:00:17.042 --> 00:00:20.157
But in real systems, all three interact.

00:00:20.157 --> 00:00:26.247
A small JSON file and a streaming feed of millions of JSON events may use the same format but require very

00:00:26.247 --> 00:00:29.357
different engineering solutions.

00:00:29.357 --> 00:00:35.277
Connect this idea to an e-commerce team preparing customer, purchase, and web-event data.

00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:40.347
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:40.347 --> 00:00:47.247
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:52.647
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:52.647 --> 00:00:57.680
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
